@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #9CA3AF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam sequenceBoxBorderColor #9CA3AF
skinparam noteBorderColor #6B7280
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F3F4F6

title Why Agent Workloads Stress LLM Serving

participant "Agent program\n(orchestration)" as prog #DCFCE7
participant "LLM server\n(GPU)" as gpu #DBEAFE
database "KV cache\n(prefix)" as kv #F3F4F6
participant "Tool\n(external)" as tool #EDE9FE

autonumber

prog -> gpu : LLM call 1 (prompt prefix)
activate gpu
gpu -> kv : build KV for the prefix
gpu --> prog : output containing a tool call
deactivate gpu

prog -> tool : run tool
activate tool
note over gpu, kv #FEE2E2
  **Tool latency window**
  Request-level serving sees the call as finished.
  GPU idles; the cache may be evicted, swapped, or recomputed (InferCept's per-pause choice).
end note
tool --> prog : tool result
deactivate tool

prog -> gpu : LLM call 2 (same prefix + result)
activate gpu
gpu -> kv : reuse prefix, or re-prefill if evicted
gpu --> prog : next output
deactivate gpu

note over prog, tool #DCFCE7
  **Where the research intervenes**
  * Prefix cache across calls: SGLang / RadixAttention
  * Pin KV with a TTL sized to the predicted tool duration: Continuum
  * Overlap tool run with prefill or decoding: Sutradhara, AsyncFC (futures)
  * Plan a DAG and run independent calls in parallel: LLMCompiler
  * Program-level scheduling: Autellix
end note
@enduml
